Paraśurāma challenges Rāma to string Vaiṣṇava bow for duel --- Daśaratha pleads with folded hands for young sons' safety --- Daśaratha recalls weapon vow, Kāśyapa gift, Mahēndra retreat, warns all die if Rāma dies --- Paraśurāma ignores Daśaratha and addresses Rāma --- Paraśurāma tells two Viśvakarman bows, Śiva bow broken, Viṣṇu bow equal --- Brahmā foments Śiva-Viṣṇu duel, gods judge Viṣṇu superior --- Paraśurāma traces Śiva bow to Dēvarāta, Viṣṇu bow through R̥cīka to Jamadagni --- Paraśurāma recalls father murder, Kṣatriya slaughter, Kāśyapa gift, Mahēndra retreat, return for broken bow